{
  "quest.381B55C984A8BD33.title": "&fResize and &bPosition",
  "quest.1A1161EF6276767F.quest_subtitle": "&oKeep a few Focus Matrices handy",
  "quest.2CA74676EAC1A040.quest_desc": [
    "MFFS machines share a system when they use the same &bFrequency&r. Set the number in each machine's interface, or place it in a &aFrequency Card&r and use that card on the machines you want to link.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click the card to generate a frequency. A &aRemote Controller&r can also link to a machine and open its interface from a distance. It still needs a working MFFS system on that frequency.",
  ],
  "quest.6600E26635FD3D0E.quest_desc": [
    "&2Speed Modules&r improve performance, &aCapacity Modules&r increase Fortron storage, and Scale Modules extend range. The exact effect depends on the machine. Check its upgrade slots and interface to see what changed.",
    "",
    "On the Deriver, Lapis Lazuli and Nether Quartz can also boost output. The boost items are consumed, so don't leave a valuable stack in the machine by accident.",
  ],
  "quest.381B55C984A8BD33.quest_desc": [
    "The Projector's directional slots control field dimensions and placement. &2Scale Modules&r change size, &aTranslation Modules&r shift the field, and Rotation Modules turn it. Each slot controls a direction, so check the arrows before adding modules.",
    "",
    "Other machines use these upgrades differently. Check the target machine's interface before assuming Scale always means a larger force field.",
  ],
  "task.635B7364CF619AF2.title": "Any Shape &aMode&r",
  "quest.6600E26635FD3D0E.title": "&aTune the System",
  "quest.1A1161EF6276767F.title": "&fMFFS Starts With &6Steel",
  "quest.56E9C123DD727E46.quest_subtitle": "&oCheck every filter before enabling it",
  "quest.56E9C123DD727E46.quest_desc": [
    "Matrix modules can block GUI access, stop block placement and breaking, prevent mob spawns, or warn players. Anti-Hostile, Anti-Friendly, and Anti-Personnel modules attack their matching targets. Confiscation can take items from player inventories.",
    "",
    "These effects can ruin someone's day, including yours. Check the Matrix filter and Identifier permissions before powering it. The Warn Module extends the warning area; it doesn't make the action area safer.",
  ],
  "quest.0089BFB911BD5E5B.title": "&dInterdiction Matrix",
  "quest.56E9C123DD727E46.title": "&fMatrix &bModules",
  "quest.711E7B6204708BD7.quest_subtitle": "&oFortron, mode, redstone",
  "task.3EE910748019C5AF.title": "Any Projector &aModule&r",
  "quest.68258EA281734B4A.title": "&fBuffer &3Fortron",
  "quest.166BA0D04A1686C7.quest_desc": [
    "Fortron is a fluid, so you can move it with the pack's fluid-handling blocks and pipes. Pump it from the Deriver or a Capacitor into a tank or machine that accepts it.",
    "",
    "The Task Screen needs the requested amount before this task completes. Check the screen's target and the pipe direction if the bar won't move.",
  ],
  "quest.0B1E459D12D11A0D.quest_subtitle": "&oThe center slot picks the mode",
  "quest.166BA0D04A1686C7.title": "&fMove &3Fortron",
  "quest.75818C9F54BD4C02.quest_subtitle": "&oThe Deriver needs FE",
  "quest.68258EA281734B4A.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFortron Capacitor&r stores Fortron and routes it between nearby MFFS machines on the same &bFrequency&r. Set the Deriver and Capacitor to the same frequency, then give both a redstone signal.",
    "",
    "The Capacitor's interface controls how it distributes Fortron. &2Speed&r affects transfer, &aCapacity&r adds storage, and Scale extends the link range.",
  ],
  "quest.56519A6A39FA9430.quest_desc": [
    "Projector modules change how a field behaves. A &bField Fusion Module&r trims overlapping blocks so multiple fields can join cleanly. A &bReinforcement Module&r protects projected field blocks from the Wither.",
    "",
    "&bDome, Glow, Shock, Silence, and Camouflage Modules&r alter the field's shape, light, contact damage, sound, or appearance. Put each module in the Projector's matrix slots and test the result somewhere safe.",
  ],
  "task.353EC1F56D14BEF5.title": "Any Field Effect &aModule&r",
  "quest.56519A6A39FA9430.quest_subtitle": "&oFuse fields or stop the Wither",
  "quest.75818C9F54BD4C02.quest_desc": [
    "The &aCoercion Deriver&r converts FE into &3Fortron&r. Feed it FE, give it a redstone signal, and set its frequency to match the rest of your system. Red means it isn't running; blue means it's working.",
    "",
    "Lapis Lazuli or Nether Quartz can boost its output, and the Deriver consumes them. Switch to Integrate mode when you want to turn Fortron back into FE.",
  ],
  "quest.0089BFB911BD5E5B.quest_subtitle": "&oSet the rules for its area",
  "quest.3435641A78B90D97.quest_desc": [
    "&bDisintegration&r breaks blocks where the field forms. Add &bCollection&r to send drops into an adjacent inventory. &bStabilization&r replaces the field with real blocks from an adjacent inventory, so keep it stocked.",
    "",
    "&bSponge&r removes fluids inside the projected area. These modules can change terrain or clear fluids. Test them away from anything you want to keep.",
  ],
  "quest.0089BFB911BD5E5B.quest_desc": [
    "The &aInterdiction Matrix&r applies its installed modules to entities and players in its action area. Add &2Scale Modules&r to extend that area, then use an &aIdentifier&r to manage player permissions.",
    "",
    "Give it a matching frequency and redstone signal before testing its rules. The Warn Module can warn unauthorized players in range; it doesn't stop the Matrix's other effects.",
  ],
  "quest.381B55C984A8BD33.quest_subtitle": "&oSlots have directions for a reason",
  "quest.1A1161EF6276767F.quest_desc": [
    "MFFS builds force fields, powered machines, and a few ways to make visitors regret wandering in. Start with &2Steel&r and a &aFocus Matrix&r. Both show up throughout the mod, so you'll want more than one.",
    "",
    "The handbook is included with this quest. Recipes show the exact ingredients; the useful part is learning how the machines share &3Fortron&r and a &bFrequency&r.",
  ],
  "quest.56519A6A39FA9430.title": "&fProjector &bModules",
  "quest.1E2A91B73A752B3B.title": "&aSet Permissions",
  "quest.1E2A91B73A752B3B.quest_desc": [
    "The &aBiometric Identifier&r uses &bIdentification Cards&r to set player permissions for force fields and Interdiction Matrices. Sneak + Right-click with a blank card to assign it to yourself, or Sneak + Right-click another player to assign it to them.",
    "",
    "Place a card in the Identifier's Rights slot, choose its permissions, then move it into a player slot. Add your own card to the Master slot. Keep sneaking until you're fully through a field, or it can still hurt you.",
  ],
  "task.564EB2A18D14814B.title": "Any Matrix &aModule&r",
  "quest.68258EA281734B4A.quest_subtitle": "&oMatch the frequency first",
  "quest.3435641A78B90D97.title": "&fField &bEffects",
  "quest.2CA74676EAC1A040.title": "&aKeep Machines in Sync",
  "quest.0B1E459D12D11A0D.quest_desc": [
    "Mode items choose the Projector's shape. Cube and Tube make box-like fields; Sphere, Cylinder, and Pyramid give you other starting outlines. Put the mode in the red center slot, then use directional &2Scale Modules&r to size it.",
    "",
    "&bCustom Mode&r records a build pattern between two selected points. Select opposite corners, then Sneak + Right-click to analyze the blocks between them. A &2Camouflage Module&r disguises the field as a block you put in the Projector's matrix.",
  ],
  "quest.711E7B6204708BD7.title": "&dProject a Field",
  "quest.1E2A91B73A752B3B.quest_subtitle": "&oGive each card only the rights it needs",
  "quest.0B1E459D12D11A0D.title": "&fChoose the &bShape",
  "quest.711E7B6204708BD7.quest_desc": [
    "Give the &aForce Field Projector&r access to &3Fortron&r on its frequency. Put a mode item in the red center slot, set the field with modules in the surrounding slots, then activate the Projector with redstone.",
    "",
    "Check the displayed Fortron cost before you start. The Projector won't build the field without enough Fortron.",
  ],
  "quest.3435641A78B90D97.quest_subtitle": "&oSome of these edit the world",
  "quest.6600E26635FD3D0E.quest_subtitle": "&oSame modules, different jobs",
  "quest.2CA74676EAC1A040.quest_subtitle": "&oFrequency Card saves the repeated trips",
  "quest.75818C9F54BD4C02.title": "&3Make Fortron",
  "quest.166BA0D04A1686C7.quest_subtitle": "&oIt's a fluid. Use fluid tools",
}